# Trivy suppressions for the worker image scan (.github/workflows/ci.yaml).
# Each entry documents a vulnerability we have evaluated and accepted; the
# bare CVE id on its own line is what actively suppresses it. Review on each
# worker-image bump and delete entries whose fix has shipped.

# --- The bundled npm CLI (/usr/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules) ships undici
# 6.29.0. CVE-2026-109869 is an undici DoS via an unhandled stream error in
# npm's own registry client (6.29.1 fixes); the worst case is one failed npm
# command on the single-tenant worker. npm 12.2.1, the worker's pin and the
# latest release, still bundles 6.29.0 - clears when an npm release bundles
# undici >= 6.29.1.
CVE-2026-109869

# --- The uv-managed CPython (/opt/python) bundles pip, whose _vendor tree pins
# msgpack==1.1.2, setuptools==70.3.0 and urllib3==2.7.0 (pip/_vendor/vendor.txt
# - Trivy reads the pins as installed packages). GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 (msgpack
# Unpacker-reuse out-of-bounds read, fixed in 1.2.1) touches only pip's
# deserialization of its own local HTTP cache. CVE-2025-47273 (setuptools
# PackageIndex path traversal, fixed in 78.1.1) lives in package_index.py,
# which pip's vendored copy does not ship - only the pkg_resources subset of
# setuptools is vendored. CVE-2026-97687 (HTTPS-proxy TLS configuration
# override) and CVE-2026-97689 (chunk-parser memory DoS), both fixed in urllib3
# 2.8.0, reach only pip's own index traffic; the worker configures no proxy.
# The pins cannot be raised independently of pip, and the latest pip (26.2.2)
# still carries all three - clears when a pip release re-vendors msgpack
# >= 1.2.1, setuptools >= 78.1.1 and urllib3 >= 2.8.0.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
